gen.clj: third-party notices

gen.clj is under the MIT License (LICENSE). Some of its files derive from
other projects and keep their own licenses. Each is listed here with its
origin; each file carries the header described below.

This file travels with what gen.clj ships: at the root of the repository,
of a jar built from it, and of the native artifact (native/'s C++ library
for 1.3.0's kernels), beside LICENSE and the license texts the entries
name. A ported Apache-2.0 file also keeps its own notice, and the
upstream project's NOTICE file, if it has one, is reproduced in its entry
(Apache License 2.0, section 4).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
How a ported file is recorded (docs/decisions.md, "1.3.0's kernels:
ported from their origins, everything around them ours")
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Before a port, its origin is checked: the upstream file's history
   (git log --follow) and the projects it credits. A kernel is ported
   from where it originated (mlx-lm's gated-delta kernels, not
   mlx-node's copies of them; kernels-community's paged attention, not
   copies that dropped its notice).

2. The ported file starts with this header, in the file's own comment
   syntax (a Clojure var holding kernel source has it as a ;; comment
   above the var, and the source string starts with it too, so that it
   travels with the kernel):

     // Ported from <project>: <URL of the file at the commit below>
     // Upstream commit: <the full commit hash>
     // License: <SPDX identifier> (Copyright <years> <holders>); see
     //          gen.clj's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES
     // Changes: <what gen.clj changed, or "none">

   An Apache-2.0 file keeps its own license header verbatim above these
   lines, and its Changes line states that the file was modified, as
   section 4(b) asks.

3. The file gets an entry below: its path in gen.clj, the project, the
   upstream path, commit and URL, the license and copyright line, and
   for Apache-2.0 the upstream NOTICE text. A license text the entries
   need that LICENSE does not already hold goes beside them (as
   test/gen/genjl/LICENSE does for Gen.jl's).

